        "en": "Forward-looking considerations vary by format. For department stores, the fact that same-store growth accelerated further in the second quarter versus an already record-setting first quarter suggests peak-out concerns are premature, with double-digit sales growth expected to continue in the second half, making the sustainability of foreign tourist spending and asset-effect driven consumption the key variable. Hypermarkets and convenience stores face structural headwinds as Gen Z-led, mobile-centric consumption trends are expected to perpetuate offline retailers' difficulties, placing the focus on omnichannel transformation and store efficiency initiatives. In the rental segment, Coway's continued diversification beyond water purifiers into mattresses and air conditioners across Malaysia and Thailand, alongside a 40% year-on-year increase in Thai rental accounts, makes the durability of overseas growth a key watch point. For trading-house style companies, new profit sources from increased gas production at Australia's Senex field and the Indonesian palm oil acquisition, combined with upcoming North American natural gas upstream exposure, point to additional energy-segment momentum, making resource and food portfolio expansion outcomes an important variable for future earnings."
