        "en": "The hotel and leisure sector encompasses tourism-consumption-linked services including casinos, duty-free retail, hotels, travel agencies, and golf/ski resorts. Individual constituents carry relatively small market capitalizations, so the sector's overall weight within the KOSPI and KOSDAQ markets remains limited, yet it is widely regarded as a bellwether for inbound tourist flows and domestic consumption trends. The sector combines companies with stable cash generation, such as Kangwon Land, Korea's sole domestic-only casino monopoly, alongside businesses directly exposed to inbound tourist demand, such as foreign-only casino operators and duty-free retailers. Since the post-pandemic tourism recovery gained momentum, earnings across the sector have broadly improved, though the pace of recovery and structural improvement differs by company. Exchange rates, air route capacity, and shifts in the nationality mix of inbound visitors are key drivers of short-term earnings volatility across the sector."
