        "en": "Korea's listed AI sector is not a single homogeneous industry but rather a thematic grouping of companies with distinct business models spanning medical AI, AI semiconductor design IP, natural language processing/translation, and generative AI/agent platforms. It is dominated by small- and mid-cap KOSDAQ names, many of which have listed relatively recently and remain in the process of proving out profitability. Medical AI firms such as Lunit generate a very high share of revenue overseas, while semiconductor IP providers such as OpenEdges Technology earn royalty and licensing income from global fabless, automotive, and defense customers. NLP-focused firms including Saltlux and Konan Technology are pursuing demand for generative AI and agentic AI solutions in Korea's public sector, financial, and defense enterprise markets. Although the sector includes a large number of listed names, individual market capitalizations are small, resulting in a limited overall weight within the broader KOSPI/KOSDAQ market, and share price behavior tends to be driven more by technology momentum and policy themes than by aggregate earnings trends."
