        "en": "The value chain broadly splits into three segments. The first is medical imaging diagnostics, exemplified by Lunit, which supplies AI-based image analysis solutions for breast and lung cancer screening to hospitals and health-check providers. The second is AI semiconductor design IP, where OpenEdges Technology licenses NPU, memory controller, and on-chip interconnect IP to fabless firms as well as automotive and defense customers, an upstream business model in which revenue is recognized before actual chip mass production. The third segment covers natural language processing, generative AI, and translation, where firms such as Saltlux, Konan Technology, and Flitto supply enterprise solutions to public sector, financial, and defense clients based on proprietary large language models or data assets. This is complemented by companies specializing in narrower niches, including Makinarocks (industrial AI), Nota (model optimization/lightweighting), Selvas AI (speech and text recognition), and JLK (medical AI). Overall revenue scale within the sector tends to be modest, and apart from a handful of larger names, many companies remain at an early business stage, resulting in relatively low industry concentration."
